                                                "sense_id": "1dcd1efa-fc08-306b-9270-f09acde77266",
                                                "text": "The security guard captured two boosters before they could exit the retail store."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f06ab844-95e2-3bf7-8568-4a6dac4ec40d",
                                        "entry_id": "1f1b86ec-6dc4-3fa1-99c9-6ba4698d328a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A booster engine fitted to a steam locomotive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfd08c9d-b656-46d7-824d-49602c645a5a",
                                                "sense_id": "f06ab844-95e2-3bf7-8568-4a6dac4ec40d",
                                                "text": "Another notable new series of locomotives, now in course of delivery to the Canadian National Railways, [...]. Fifteen are being built by the Montreal Locomotive Works Limited, and ten by the Canadian Locomotive Company, of Kingston, Ontario; the former are being provided with boosters and the latter are not."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "481e5507-95b0-4530-aadb-a4d8905fc0ce",
                                                "sense_id": "f06ab844-95e2-3bf7-8568-4a6dac4ec40d",
                                                "text": "Also in 1939, six 4-8-4s, classified \"Kb\" because they have boosters, were built at Hillside for service between Christchurch and Arthurs Pass."
                                            }
                                        ]
